# MathemAct environment template. Copy to .env for local development:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything in this file is PUBLIC BY DESIGN.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Astro inlines any PUBLIC_-prefixed variable into the built JavaScript, so all three
# values below are readable by anyone who views source on the deployed site. That is
# correct and intended:
#
#   * The Supabase project URL is just an address.
#   * The Supabase anon key identifies the *anonymous role*, not a user. It grants nothing
#     on its own — row level security decides what that role may read and write. Every
#     Supabase browser client in existence ships this key.
#   * The Turnstile site key is meant to appear in the widget's markup.
#
# Because they are public, they are also stored as GitHub Actions *variables* rather than
# secrets, so the CI logs stay readable. See .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These three must NEVER appear in this repository, in .env, or in Actions logs:
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   bypasses row level security entirely — full read and write
#                               on every table. Lives only in GitHub Actions secrets, used
#                               by the nightly export job.
#   Brevo SMTP key              lives only in the Supabase dashboard, under
#                               Authentication → SMTP settings. Supabase sends the mail,
#                               we never do.
#   Turnstile SECRET key        lives only in the Supabase dashboard, under
#                               Authentication → CAPTCHA settings. A static site has no
#                               server, so Supabase Auth verifies the token for us.
#
# If a task appears to need one of these in the client, the design is wrong. Stop.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase project (EU region, project ref fgnmafmzracdytpfqpel)
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://fgnmafmzracdytpfqpel.supabase.co

# Supabase publishable / anon key.
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API keys → anon public
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_FEvJMhQX8Ts79cvsRDsb1Q_ZaRzwQ1q

# Cloudflare Turnstile site key.
# Cloudflare dashboard → Turnstile → your widget → Site Key
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAAEPDYKvpXDAXqQT9
